CONTEXT BareComplement
-- A rule with a bare complement on the left of the inclusion: its violation
-- term -r /\ -s contains no complement-free member, so there is no anchor
-- and the Cartesian product V[A*B] is semantically necessary. The compiler
-- must report this (warning; exit 46 under --fail-on-cartesian-product).
RELATION r[A*B]
RELATION s[A*B]
RULE noAnchor : -r |- s
ENDCONTEXT
